{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":320819,"ns":0,"title":"Cantor function","extract":"In mathematics, the Cantor function is an example of a  function that is continuous, but not absolutely continuous. It is a notorious counterexample in analysis, because it challenges naive intuitions about continuity, derivative, and measure.","description":"Continuous function that is not absolutely continuous","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}